[en.FOCUS_C18_OLD_YIN]
Old Yin

[en.FOCUS_C18_OLD_YIN_desc]
The public is the first, then comes the state, and the leader comes last. The leader of the Kirins must always remember that the civilization of the Kirins does not lie within the prosperity of buildings, but within every single Kirin’s heart.\nThe scorching sun cannot always shine on the earth alone, at midnight, the darkest moment, only the countless stars in the sky can dispel the darkness. The stars are invisible in the daytime, but they must not be forgotten or ignored. After all, the sun is just one of the stars.

[zh.FOCUS_C18_OLD_YIN]
太阴

[zh.FOCUS_C18_OLD_YIN_desc]
民为贵，社稷次之，君为轻。麒麟的领袖必须时刻牢记，麒麟族的文明不在于高楼大厦，而在于每一只麒麟的心中。\n烈日不能永远独自照耀大地，在午夜之时，至暗之刻唯有漫天的群星才能驱散黑暗。群星在白日不见踪迹，但绝不能忘记和忽视。毕竟，太阳本也只是群星中的一个。

